TailGauge is a port of the first-party Tailscale panel plugin that ships with
Omarchy 4 (Quattro), from Hyprland/Quickshell to KDE Plasma 6 and GNOME Shell.

Upstream: https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy (MIT, Copyright (c) David
Heinemeier Hansson), branch `quattro`:

  shell/plugins/panels/tailscale/{Model.js,Service.qml,Panel.qml,TailscaleIcon.qml}
  bin/omarchy-tailscale-send
  bin/omarchy-tailscale-receive
  default/systemd/user/omarchy-tailscale-receive.service

What was carried over and what was rewritten:

  shared/model.js
      Derived from Model.js, near-verbatim. The status, account and exit-node
      parsing, the Mullvad region grouping and the Taildrop capability checks
      are upstream's. Added here: osIconName, the recent-region helpers that
      Panel.qml kept inline, and the shell-quoting helpers Plasma needs.

  bin/tailgauge-send, bin/tailgauge-receive
      Derived from the omarchy-tailscale-* scripts. The Taildrop staging and
      link(2) name-claiming logic is upstream's; the file chooser and the
      notification helper are replaced with desktop-neutral equivalents.

  plasma/, gnome/
      Rewritten. Service.qml's state machine (optimistic toggle, poll
      watchdog, startup ramp, login URL scraping) is reproduced against
      Plasma5Support.DataSource and Gio.Subprocess respectively; Panel.qml's
      layout and keyboard model are reproduced against Plasma Components and
      St/PopupMenu. No Quickshell code is used.

